From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PR #3 audit: complete order records, status ordering,
 Redis-outage safety, reconcile/fulfil tools, tests, docs

Findings fixed:
- Orders lacked what fulfilment needs: now record shipping name/address, PaymentIntent id,
  itemized snapshot, Stripe subtotal/total, and a fulfilment status (unfulfilled -> shipped|cancelled)
- paid and payment_failed shared a rank, so a replayed 'failed' event could overwrite a paid
  order: paid now outranks payment_failed
- Checkout rate-limit and Redis calls sat outside the try block: a Redis outage became an
  unhandled 500. Route logic moved to lib/commerce/http.ts, outages now return a safe 503
- Live mode now requires a configured https NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL for Stripe return links
  instead of deriving them from the request Host header
- Structured JSON webhook logs with no customer data
- New: pnpm inventory fulfill / reconcile [--apply] (rebuilds paid Stripe sessions missing from Redis)
- tests/ and scripts/ are now type-checked (they were excluded)
- 49 new tests (95 total): tampered price/SKU/size/colour/qty, Redis outage, webhook failing
  halfway then retried, route-level signature rejection, order completeness, status ordering,
  fulfilment, reconcile. Mutation-checked: each fix's test fails when the fix is reverted
- Smoke test extended to 15 steps incl. the real CLI against real Redis
- docs/CHECKOUT.md: lifecycle, order data, new commands, launch blockers

